   =========================================================
   CSS OVERFLOW
   =========================================================

   DEFINITION:
   The overflow property controls when content
   is larger than its container.

   It decides whether extra content is:
   - Visible
   - Hidden
   - Scrollable



 =========================================================
   OVERFLOW VALUES
   ========================================================= 

 1. visible (default)
   -> Content overflows outside the container
   ->  No clipping, no scrollbars

        .visible {
            overflow: visible;
        }

 2. hidden
  -> Extra content is clipped
  -> Content outside the box is0000 not visible

        .hidden {
            overflow: hidden;
        }

 3. scroll
  -> Scrollbars are always shown
  -> Allows scrolling even if content fits

        .scroll {
            overflow: scroll;
        }

 4. auto
   -> Scrollbars appear only when content overflows
   -> Most commonly used value

        .auto {
            overflow: auto;
        }


 =========================================================
   HORIZONTAL & VERTICAL OVERFLOW
   ========================================================= 


overflow-x → controls left & right overflow
overflow-y → controls top & bottom overflow


.axis-control {
    overflow-x: auto;    horizontal scroll if needed 
    overflow-y: hidden;  vertical content clipped 
}


 =========================================================
   IMPORTANT NOTES
   =========================================================

   • Overflow works only when width and/or height is set
   • Default overflow value is visible
   • overflow: hidden is commonly used to:
       - Crop images
       - Clear floating elements
       - Hide unwanted content
   • overflow: auto is best for responsive layouts
   • overflow can prevent margin collapsing in some cases



 =========================================================
   SIMPLE PRACTICE BOX
   ========================================================= 

.box {
    width: 220px;
    height: 100px;
    padding: 10px;
    border: 2px solid #333;
    overflow: auto;
}

/* =========================================================
   CSS OVERFLOW – SCROLLBAR SUMMARY

   • overflow controls how extra content behaves
   • overflow: scroll always shows BOTH scrollbars
       - horizontal scrollbar → bottom (left ↔ right)
       - vertical scrollbar   → right  (up ↕ down)

   • To show ONLY ONE scrollbar, use axis-specific properties:
       - overflow-x controls horizontal (bottom) scrollbar
       - overflow-y controls vertical (right) scrollbar

   • Examples:
       overflow-x: scroll;
       overflow-y: hidden;   → only bottom scrollbar

       overflow-y: scroll;
       overflow-x: hidden;   → only right scrollbar

   • overflow: auto shows scrollbars only when needed
   • overflow works only when width and/or height is set

   ========================================================= */
